189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 106 0 R
/T (3.2 Camera Navigation relies on a Raspberry Pi Camera v2 \(8MP\), connected directly to the Pi 5's CSI camera port via ribbon cable. The image feed is processed to estimate what percentage of the frame is taken up by the left wall versus the right wall; the difference between the two is used as the main steering error signal to keep the robot centered between the walls. The same camera is used to detect and classify the red/green traffic-sign pillars in the Obstacle Challenge. 8MP resolution was chosen as enough to reliably estimate wall coverage and pillar colour/side at the frame rates needed, without producing more data than the Pi 5 needs to process per frame. In the final design the camera was moved back slightly and mounted higher on the tower to improve this view.)
/E (3.2 Camera Navigation relies on a Raspberry Pi Camera v2 \(8MP\), connected directly to the Pi 5's CSI camera port via ribbon cable. The image feed is processed to estimate what percentage of the frame is taken up by the left wall versus the right wall; the difference between the two is used as the main steering error signal to keep the robot centered between the walls. The same camera is used to detect and classify the red/green traffic-sign pillars in the Obstacle Challenge. 8MP resolution was chosen as enough to reliably estimate wall coverage and pillar colour/side at the frame rates needed, without producing more data than the Pi 5 needs to process per frame. In the final design the camera was moved back slightly and mounted higher on the tower to improve this view.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
