191 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 106 0 R
/T (3.4 Power Supply Power is split across two isolated rails. A Joyroom 10,000 mAh fast-charging powerbank \(rated up to 22.5 W, treated as a hard design constraint\) supplies the entire logic side: the Raspberry Pi 5,camera, both ultrasonic sensors, and the supporting LED/button circuit described below. A separate 4x 18650 Li-ion battery pack \(4 x 3.7V, ~14.8V nominal, ~16.8V full / ~12V cutoff\) supplies the drive side of the vehicle, kept completely isolated from the 5V logic rail to avoid motor current/noise or voltage sag affecting the electronics. The 10,000 mAh powerbank was sized to cover a full competition day of practice plus rounds, with a digital display to monitor remaining charge betweenrounds and fast-charge support to top up quickly during breaks.)
/E (3.4 Power Supply Power is split across two isolated rails. A Joyroom 10,000 mAh fast-charging powerbank \(rated up to 22.5 W, treated as a hard design constraint\) supplies the entire logic side: the Raspberry Pi 5,camera, both ultrasonic sensors, and the supporting LED/button circuit described below. A separate 4x 18650 Li-ion battery pack \(4 x 3.7V, ~14.8V nominal, ~16.8V full / ~12V cutoff\) supplies the drive side of the vehicle, kept completely isolated from the 5V logic rail to avoid motor current/noise or voltage sag affecting the electronics. The 10,000 mAh powerbank was sized to cover a full competition day of practice plus rounds, with a digital display to monitor remaining charge betweenrounds and fast-charge support to top up quickly during breaks.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 106 0 R
/T (3.5 Thermal Management A 5V cooling fan, powered from the logic-side powerbank, provides active cooling for the Raspberry Pi 5. The Pi 5 runs noticeably hotter than previous Pi models under sustained camera-processing load; without active cooling, thermal throttling would slow down frame-processing rate mid-round. In the final design the fan was moved to sit on top of the Pi 5 instead of underneath it, for better airflow.)
/E (3.5 Thermal Management A 5V cooling fan, powered from the logic-side powerbank, provides active cooling for the Raspberry Pi 5. The Pi 5 runs noticeably hotter than previous Pi models under sustained camera-processing load; without active cooling, thermal throttling would slow down frame-processing rate mid-round. In the final design the fan was moved to sit on top of the Pi 5 instead of underneath it, for better airflow.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
